{"data": [{"author_id": "68746721", "created_at": "2026-11-02T00:01:27.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117044380532097088"], "id": "2117044380532097088", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 11, "impression_count": 25596, "like_count": 44, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 9, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Do I know anyone who knows anything about cyanotype printmaking?", "url": "https://x.com/fchollet/status/2117044380532097088"}, {"author_id": "68746721", "created_at": "2026-11-01T23:43:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117039855012389214"], "id": "2117039855012389214", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 311, "impression_count": 87820, "like_count": 1877, "quote_count": 34, "reply_count": 183, "retweet_count": 153}, "text": "Evolution doesn't benchmaxx. It optimizes for generality and robustness, because overspecialization makes a species fragile when the environment inevitably shifts.", "url": "https://x.com/fchollet/status/2117039855012389214"}, {"author_id": "1214528593", "created_at": "2026-11-01T23:35:44.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117037906892341296"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/3oTc6eclK3", "end": 35, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2117037906892341296/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2117037904560304128", "start": 12, "url": "https://t.co/3oTc6eclK3"}]}, "id": "2117037906892341296", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 2897, "like_count": 18, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "“Typically” https://t.co/3oTc6eclK3", "url": "https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2117037906892341296"}, {"author_id": "332617373", "created_at": "2026-11-01T21:03:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116999606336737372"], "id": "2116999606336737372", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 34481, "like_count": 156, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 27, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "Ah, the \"joys\" of being a New York Jets fan...\nThe team scored 30 points for the first time in 17 games, snapping the NFL’s longest streak. They even put points on the board in their first six possessions for the first time since 2007.\n...And yet, they still lost to the Raiders.", "url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2116999606336737372"}, {"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-11-01T20:16:07.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116987671939875319"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/alexolegimas/s…", "end": 299, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/alexolegimas/status/2116967827773030602", "start": 276, "url": "https://t.co/9qOAa353y2"}]}, "id": "2116987671939875319", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 120, "impression_count": 40483, "like_count": 760, "quote_count": 25, "reply_count": 247, "retweet_count": 39}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116967827773030602", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "GPT-4 could do 4 minutes of independent work with a 50% chance of success.\n\nCurrent models can do multiple weeks of work, and January 2026 is a reasonable cut-off for the moment agentic work started.\n\nLarge productivity impacts before that would mostly be confined to coding. https://t.co/9qOAa353y2", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2116987671939875319"}, {"author_id": "332617373", "created_at": "2026-11-01T19:51:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116981393594908878"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 110, "start": 92, "tag": "thalibychefprasad"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/pwAeyLwU2b", "end": 134, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2116981393594908878/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116981197419028481", "start": 111, "url": "https://t.co/pwAeyLwU2b"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/pwAeyLwU2b", "end": 134, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2116981393594908878/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116981197410627584", "start": 111, "url": "https://t.co/pwAeyLwU2b"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/pwAeyLwU2b", "end": 134, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2116981393594908878/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116981197419012097", "start": 111, "url": "https://t.co/pwAeyLwU2b"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/pwAeyLwU2b", "end": 134, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2116981393594908878/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116981197393821696", "start": 111, "url": "https://t.co/pwAeyLwU2b"}]}, "id": "2116981393594908878", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 10, "impression_count": 52425, "like_count": 271, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 13, "retweet_count": 8}, "text": "Our thanks to Chef Prasad for an amazing meal at \"Thali by Chef Prasad.\"\n@thalibychefprasad #thalibychefprasad https://t.co/pwAeyLwU2b", "url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2116981393594908878"}, {"author_id": "332617373", "created_at": "2026-11-01T19:07:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116970296523547108"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/8ts3e3y0eW", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2116970296523547108/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116970292123774976", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/8ts3e3y0eW"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/8ts3e3y0eW", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2116970296523547108/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116970292157263872", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/8ts3e3y0eW"}]}, "id": "2116970296523547108", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 34, "impression_count": 33761, "like_count": 194, "quote_count": 5, "reply_count": 17, "retweet_count": 33}, "text": "While on the topic of dispersion within asset classes, this from the FT on high yield bonds in Europe and the US:\n\"While the yield investors demand to hold the weakest junk-rated issuers has widened, so has the gap between those companies and their higher-rated junk market peers. https://t.co/8ts3e3y0eW", "url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2116970296523547108"}, {"author_id": "321536046", "created_at": "2026-11-01T19:00:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116968584731599298"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 176, "start": 168, "tag": "TEC2026"}], "mentions": [{"end": 167, "id": "16561802", "start": 157, "username": "nabe_econ"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/gJj8yaqQgL", "end": 200, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/BEA_News/status/2116968584731599298/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116968573889314816", "start": 177, "url": "https://t.co/gJj8yaqQgL"}]}, "id": "2116968584731599298", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 991, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Hey, San Diego! BEA is at the NABE Tech Economics Conference through Wednesday. Stop by our booth to learn about tools for accessing and analyzing BEA data. @nabe_econ #TEC2026 https://t.co/gJj8yaqQgL", "url": "https://x.com/BEA_News/status/2116968584731599298"}, {"author_id": "68746721", "created_at": "2026-11-01T18:37:54.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116962954877014152"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/T69tbG565E", "end": 77, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/fchollet/status/2116962954877014152/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116962940607959040", "start": 54, "url": "https://t.co/T69tbG565E"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/T69tbG565E", "end": 77, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/fchollet/status/2116962954877014152/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116962948778545152", "start": 54, "url": "https://t.co/T69tbG565E"}]}, "id": "2116962954877014152", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 9, "impression_count": 24155, "like_count": 202, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 27, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "I got a fun birthday present from the team at Ndea ❤️ https://t.co/T69tbG565E", "url": "https://x.com/fchollet/status/2116962954877014152"}, {"author_id": "279036722", "created_at": "2026-11-01T18:32:31.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116961600296935779"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/PFcJJHYMGI", "end": 188, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2116961600296935779/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116961598539497472", "start": 165, "url": "https://t.co/PFcJJHYMGI"}]}, "id": "2116961600296935779", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 13481, "like_count": 62, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Two students share their terrifying Halloween costumes with me. One went as David Laibson and one went as a much cooler version of me. Can you guess which is which? https://t.co/PFcJJHYMGI", "url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2116961600296935779"}, {"author_id": "332617373", "created_at": "2026-11-01T17:43:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116949137744683343"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/23kB2XCKxE", "end": 295, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2116949137744683343/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116949067422941184", "start": 272, "url": "https://t.co/23kB2XCKxE"}]}, "id": "2116949137744683343", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 27, "impression_count": 32894, "like_count": 172, "quote_count": 6, "reply_count": 26, "retweet_count": 27}, "text": "Please find below the usual monthly performance snapshot across major assets and asset classes.\nOctober was characterized by significant dispersion, both across asset classes and within them.\nOf note:\n• Marked Nasdaq underperformance relative to both the Dow and European https://t.co/23kB2XCKxE", "url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2116949137744683343"}, {"author_id": "59603406", "created_at": "2026-11-01T16:20:35.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116928398652068196"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/jasonfurman/st…", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/jasonfurman/status/2116898249764192493", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/BDmqeMmZny"}]}, "id": "2116928398652068196", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 33, "impression_count": 57415, "like_count": 179, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 17, "retweet_count": 23}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116898249764192493", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "“I can think of people I know who overrely on AI and produce slop they don’t understand. But I can think of many more people—including some economists and think tankers—whose error goes in the opposite direction: underusing the technology in ways that lead them to make too many https://t.co/BDmqeMmZny", "url": "https://x.com/NickTimiraos/status/2116928398652068196"}, {"author_id": "612896910", "created_at": "2026-11-01T16:15:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116926992264396895"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 94, "start": 86, "tag": "BLSdata"}], "urls": [{"description": "The .gov means it's official. Federal government websites often end in .gov or .mil. Before sharing sensitive information, make sure you're on a federal government site. The site is secure. The https:// ensures that you are connecting to the official website and that any information you provide is encrypted and transmitted securely. The reality television show, Survivor, which premiered in 2000, is currently airing its 51st season. It features contestants competing in challenges and voting each other out", "display_url": "bls.gov/opub/ted/2026/…", "end": 85, "expanded_url": "https://www.bls.gov/opub/ted/2026/outlast-state-establishment-survival-rates-from-2000-to-2026.htm", "images": [{"height": 126, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2116188727626420225/YRbH-WvP?format=png&name=orig", "width": 228}, {"height": 126, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2116188727626420225/YRbH-WvP?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 126}], "start": 62, "status": 200, "title": "Outlast: State establishment survival rates from 2000 to 2026 : The Economics Daily : U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics", "unwound_url": "https://www.bls.gov/opub/ted/2026/outlast-state-establishment-survival-rates-from-2000-to-2026.htm", "url": "https://t.co/7sHqQY0aAx"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/acO9BbJRvQ", "end": 118, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/BLS_gov/status/2116926992264396895/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116297592581623808", "start": 95, "url": "https://t.co/acO9BbJRvQ"}]}, "id": "2116926992264396895", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 13268, "like_count": 9, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 5}, "text": "Outlast: State establishment survival rates from 2000 to 2026 https://t.co/7sHqQY0aAx #BLSdata https://t.co/acO9BbJRvQ", "url": "https://x.com/BLS_gov/status/2116926992264396895"}, {"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-11-01T15:27:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116915149546389960"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/emollick/statu…", "end": 244, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/emollick/status/2116905564680687831", "start": 221, "url": "https://t.co/G1HuB5Nkpp"}]}, "id": "2116915149546389960", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 64, "impression_count": 38616, "like_count": 374, "quote_count": 8, "reply_count": 82, "retweet_count": 10}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116905564680687831", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "This post is a reverse CAPTCHA.\n\nLook at the replies, AIs love talking about the Oxyrhynchus Papyri, and I would be willing to guess that only a very small proportion of humans have, and most of them will spell it wrong. https://t.co/G1HuB5Nkpp", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2116915149546389960"}, {"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-11-01T14:58:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116907715683319897"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/iNOAZ43gaA", "end": 295, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2116907715683319897/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116907711719727104", "start": 272, "url": "https://t.co/iNOAZ43gaA"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/iNOAZ43gaA", "end": 295, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2116907715683319897/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116907711711387648", "start": 272, "url": "https://t.co/iNOAZ43gaA"}]}, "id": "2116907715683319897", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 28, "impression_count": 25323, "like_count": 262, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 75, "retweet_count": 13}, "text": "It is interesting to watch (and painful to read) the rapid evolution of slopreplybots in my comments. Now the latest trend is making extremely lame jokes, which seems to get them more likes, maybe sometimes even from humans. I suppose it is better than the “ask a leading https://t.co/iNOAZ43gaA", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2116907715683319897"}, {"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-11-01T14:49:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116905564680687831"], "id": "2116905564680687831", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 37, "impression_count": 51934, "like_count": 163, "quote_count": 8, "reply_count": 106, "retweet_count": 7}, "text": "A bunch of funded projects to unblock some long-standing backlogs in translations using AI would be interesting; especially when AI models can do a reasonable first pass at interpretation &amp; significance, not just translation. There are major repositories of untranslated ancient", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2116905564680687831"}, {"author_id": "279036722", "created_at": "2026-11-01T14:20:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116898249764192493"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 24, "id": "21399270", "start": 14, "username": "neilirwin"}], "urls": [{"description": "Why I still think AI could do most of what the Council of Economic Advisers did, and what that means for the people who learn by doing that work.", "display_url": "econvitals.org/posts/2026-11-…", "end": 275, "expanded_url": "https://econvitals.org/posts/2026-11-01-ai-first-job/", "images": [{"height": 630, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2116893856641826816/ErLMiLbD?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2116893856641826816/ErLMiLbD?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 252, "status": 200, "title": "AI Could Do My First Job. Not My Last.", "unwound_url": "https://econvitals.org/posts/2026-11-01-ai-first-job/", "url": "https://t.co/LqGYzLShPp"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/yfOEpt96Eh", "end": 299, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2116898249764192493/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116892318775025664", "start": 276, "url": "https://t.co/yfOEpt96Eh"}]}, "id": "2116898249764192493", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 64, "impression_count": 77753, "like_count": 87, "quote_count": 10, "reply_count": 20, "retweet_count": 24}, "text": "My comment to @neilirwin about 20 CEA staff being replaceable by AI generated discussion. My followup essay on the issue &amp; what it means for the future of work, training and the pipeline.\n\nWe shouldn't avert our gaze from the tough issues we face. https://t.co/LqGYzLShPp https://t.co/yfOEpt96Eh", "url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2116898249764192493"}, {"author_id": "279036722", "created_at": "2026-11-01T12:29:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116870216302957043"], "id": "2116870216302957043", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 37, "impression_count": 42609, "like_count": 165, "quote_count": 5, "reply_count": 11, "retweet_count": 16}, "text": "My thought on the role of growth in solving fiscal problems:\n\n1. I'm in favor of dynamic scoring for both tax &amp; spending plans--you should take into account the best estimate of impact on budget.\n\n2. Dynamic scoring needs to be done by CBO/JCT, they're generally unbiased and", "url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2116870216302957043"}, {"author_id": "25098482", "created_at": "2026-11-01T11:00:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116847838500175909"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Global resilience was tested in fiscal year 2026 by growing fiscal pressures, AI deployment and disruption, strains on still-resilient trade, and new frontiers for digital finance. The Report shows how the IMF supported its 191 members in navigating a precarious world.", "display_url": "imf.org/annual-report/…", "end": 249, "expanded_url": "https://www.imf.org/annual-report/2026?cid=sm-com-x-ARIEA2026001", "images": [{"height": 1597, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2116847805952401408/S3KFyWkH?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 2400}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2116847805952401408/S3KFyWkH?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 226, "status": 200, "title": "The 2026 IMF Annual Report: Navigating a Precarious World", "unwound_url": "https://www.imf.org/annual-report/2026/?cid=sm-com-x-ARIEA2026001", "url": "https://t.co/FIzm24lGXP"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/o6K1zDuldj", "end": 273, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2116847838500175909/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116847739099385857", "start": 250, "url": "https://t.co/o6K1zDuldj"}]}, "id": "2116847838500175909", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 16, "impression_count": 20350, "like_count": 84, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 12, "retweet_count": 21}, "text": "The 2026 IMF Annual Report, Navigating a Precarious World, covers the International Monetary Fund’s work from May 2025 through April 2026. \n\nRead it in any of eight languages. \n\nExplore the forces shaping the global economy: \nhttps://t.co/FIzm24lGXP https://t.co/o6K1zDuldj", "url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2116847838500175909"}, {"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-11-01T02:47:15.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116723717829230932"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/robocurve/stat…", "end": 308, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/robocurve/status/2116704239003349503", "start": 285, "url": "https://t.co/LR20VgWQta"}]}, "id": "2116723717829230932", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 186, "impression_count": 53548, "like_count": 701, "quote_count": 20, "reply_count": 202, "retweet_count": 55}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116704239003349503", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "This is both neat &amp; a sign of why it is proving to be so hard to isolate agents from each other. They share a common \"brain\" which means they don't have a lot of trouble recognizing creative communication solutions generated by other AIs\n\nWonder if it works across model families? https://t.co/LR20VgWQta", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2116723717829230932"}, {"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-11-01T02:40:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116721995178225799"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/emollick/statu…", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/emollick/status/1737288153432469744", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/SXUkpgGEQc"}]}, "id": "2116721995178225799", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 91, "impression_count": 64649, "like_count": 865, "quote_count": 17, "reply_count": 132, "retweet_count": 29}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "1737288153432469744", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Less than three years ago, GPT-4 was the best model in the world, as it had been for a year, and we were all speculating whether there was some unique secret method that OpenAI had or whether GPT-4 was just as good as LLMs would ever get.\n\n(The answer to both questions was \"no\") https://t.co/SXUkpgGEQc", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2116721995178225799"}, {"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-10-31T23:57:43.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116681050747248955"], "id": "2116681050747248955", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 122, "impression_count": 78890, "like_count": 866, "quote_count": 23, "reply_count": 230, "retweet_count": 14}, "text": "The Pro series of GPT models continues to be really impressive for one-shot problems that involve complex calculations, references, or sophisticated ideas.\n\nIt isn't particularly fast (or particularly pleasant) but GPT-6 Pro gives that \"ask one question of the great oracle\" feel.", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2116681050747248955"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "68746721", "name": "François Chollet", "username": "fchollet"}, {"id": "1214528593", "name": "Miles Brundage", "username": "Miles_Brundage"}, {"id": "332617373", "name": "Mohamed A. El-Erian", "username": "elerianm"}, {"id": "39125788", "name": "Ethan Mollick", "username": "emollick"}, {"id": "321536046", "name": "BEA News", "username": "BEA_News"}, {"id": "279036722", "name": "Jason Furman", "username": "jasonfurman"}, {"id": "59603406", "name": "Nick Timiraos", "username": "NickTimiraos"}, {"id": "612896910", "name": "BLS-Labor Statistics", "username": "BLS_gov"}, {"id": "25098482", "name": "IMF", "username": "IMFNews"}]}, "meta": {"newest_id": "2117044380532097088", "next_token": "b26v89c19zqg8o3juzly3cakuki1rpyi0oet9xlwx4rct", "oldest_id": "2116681050747248955", "result_count": 22}}
